### Equation Used for WCD:
The worst-case delay (WCD) for each flow is calculated as:
\[
WCD_f = \sum_{h \in \text{path}} D_f^h + \text{propagation delay} \times \text{hop count} + \text{switching delay} \times \text{hop count}
\]
where \( D_f^h \) is the horizontal deviation (per-hop delay) computed via Network Calculus:
\[
D_f^h = hDev(\alpha_{M_i}^h, \beta_{M_i}^h)
\]
with \(\alpha_{M_i}^h\) being the aggregate arrival curve and \(\beta_{M_i}^h\) the CBS service curve.

